%U A397783 17208,0,12852,17664,26224,0,21608,0,32588,35408,23100,0,43260,21168,37808,39680,54464,0,51812,49920
%N A397783 Sum of squares of differences of consecutive terms of n/gcd(n,k), k = 1..n-1.
%C A397783 Equivalently, a(n) is the sum of squared differences of consecutive entries among the first n-1 entries of row n of A054531, whose k-th entry is n/gcd(n,k).
%C A397783 Since n/gcd(n,k) is the additive order of k in Z/nZ, a(n) is the sum of squared differences of the additive orders of consecutive nonzero residues 1..n-1.
%C A397783 For n > 1, a(n) = 0 if and only if n is prime. For prime n, all n-1 terms equal n. For composite n, some interior term is smaller than n, whereas the first and last terms equal n.
%C A397783 All terms are even, since n/gcd(n,k) = n/gcd(n,n-k) and the consecutive squared differences occur in symmetric pairs.
%F A397783 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n-2} (n/gcd(n,k+1) - n/gcd(n,k))^2.
%F A397783 a(p^r) = 2*(p-1)*Sum_{i=1..r-1} p^(i-1)*(p^r-p^i)^2, p prime, r >= 1.
%F A397783 a(2*p) = 2*(p-1)*(p-2)*(p+2), p odd prime.
%F A397783 a(p) = 0 for prime p.
%e A397783 For n = 6, the first n-1 terms n/gcd(n,k) are 6, 3, 2, 3, 6. Hence a(6) = (6-3)^2 + (3-2)^2 + (2-3)^2 + (3-6)^2 = 20.
%e A397783 For n = 7, the corresponding terms are 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, so a(7) = 0.
%o A397783 (Python)
%o A397783 from math import gcd
%o A397783 def a(n):
%o A397783     return sum((n//gcd(n, k+1) - n//gcd(n, k))**2 for k in range(1, n-1))
%o A397783 (PARI) a(n) = sum(k=1, n-2, (n/gcd(n,k+1) - n/gcd(n,k))^2); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Oct 14 2026
